<title>FRANCE: EU did not open export tenders at grain meeting.</title>
<headline>EU did not open export tenders at grain meeting.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union did not open export tenders for 1997/98 (July/June) at the weekly cereals management committee meeting in Brussels on Thursday, an EU official said.</p>
<p>No decision to open the tenders had been expected after the European Commission said on Tuesday it was in no hurry to launch the export mechanism pending more harvest information.</p>
<p>The effect was to keep the European Union off the world grain market for at least another few weeks. Any decision to open the tenders would take several weeks to implement and need not then lead to actual subsidies being granted straight away.</p>
</text>
